From 95b2a6e31b3f44b458bc8b13931048e9306744b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moritz Wegner <moritzwegner46@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:55:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: SharedDeck client mode for display computers, RMP
 and clock

On a SharedDeck client the computers inside display instruments must not
compute either, otherwise they keep writing values that differ from the
mirrored host state (seen as repeated halts):

- PFD PseudoDmc, OANS: outputs come from the host
- RMP: key presses are executed by the host's RMP only
- clock chrono/ET: show the host's timers, keys executed by the host
- shared isSharedDeckClient() helper in fbw-common

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
